{{smaller block|<poem>That dore can noon ''ussher'' shette.</poem>
{{right|''Gower'', Conf. Amant., i.}}}}
{{smaller block|<poem>The sable Night dis-lodged; and now began
Aurora’s ''Vsher'' with his windy Fan
Gently to shake the Woods on every side.</poem>
{{right|''Sylvester'', tr. of Du Bartas’s Weeks, ii., The Fathers.}}}}
{{smaller block|<poem>''P. jun.'' Art thou her grace’s steward?
''Bro.'' No, her ''usher'', sir.
''P. jun.'' What, of the hall? thou hast a sweeping face;
Thy beard is like a broom.</poem>
{{right|''B. Jonson'', Staple of News, ii.}}}}
'''2.''' An under-teacher, or assistant to a schoolmaster or principal teacher.
